!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Transient brain ischemia, induced by middle cerebral artery occlusion (MCAO), was generated in male mice between 8 and 24 weeks of age, with a weight range of 20 to 30 g. Anesthesia was induced by 3% isoflurane with a mixture of 70% nitrous oxide and 30% oxygen, and maintained by 1% isoflurane during the operation. Silicone-coated monofilaments were inserted through the common carotid artery to occlude the origin of the middle cerebral artery. Reperfusion was facilitated by withdrawing the inserted monofilaments 60 minutes after MCAO. Head temperature was maintained at 36°C. Inclusion criteria required confirmation of a >60% reduction in cerebral blood flow using laser Doppler flowmetry. Sham-operated mice underwent the same surgical procedure without occlusion.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = All mice were maintained in a conventional facility at the Institute of Science Tokyo or Tokyo Metropolitan Institute of Medical Science in Tokyo, Japan. All experiments were approved by the Institutional Animal Research Committee of the Institute of Science Tokyo (approval number: A2025-011C2) and Tokyo Metropolitan Institute of Medical Science (approval number: 21-004). C57BL/6J mice were used for WT mice.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For microglia samples: Sham-operated mice or mice after MCAO were transcardially perfused with saline, and then the forebrain was removed. After homogenization with RPMI-1640, 1 mg ml–1 collagenase (Sigma-Aldrich) and 50 mg ml–1 DNase I (Sigma-Aldrich) were added to the homogenates. Brain homogenates were digested for 25 min and subjected to Percoll (GE Healthcare) gradient centrifugation. From the interlayer between 37% and 70% Percoll, cells were isolated and stained with anti-CD45 FITC (30-F11, eBioscience), anti-CD11b PerCP-Cy5.5 (M1/70, eBioscience), and anti-CD31 PE/Cyanine7 (390, eBioscience). CD45(int)CD11b(int) cells were sorted using a FACSAria III cell sorter (BD/Thermo Fisher Scientific). For whole brain cell samples: Brain cells including neurons were isolated from adult ischemic brain according to the protocol established in the Allen Institute (Tasic et al., Nature 2018); the detailed experimental method was described previously (Nakamura et al., Neuron 2023).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Brain cells including neurons were isolated from adult ischemic brain according to the protocol established in the Allen Institute (Tasic et al., Nature 2018); the detailed experimental method was described previously (Nakamura et al., Neuron 2023). Single CD45(int)CD11b(int) cells or brain cells were loaded onto chromium chips with a capture target of 2,000 to 10,000 cells per sample. Libraries were prepared using Chromium Next GEM Single Cell 5′ Reagent Kits v2 (10x Genomics) for CD45(int)CD11b(int) cells or Chromium Next GEM Single-cell 3′ Reagent Kits v3.1 (10x Genomics) for brain cells, according to the manufacturer's protocol. On a DNBSEQ-G400 sequencer (MGI), obtained libraries were sequenced with a targeted sequencing depth of more than 50,000 read pairs per cell.
!Sample_description = Library name: scRNA_Mouse_Microglia_Day56_ASOcontrol
!Sample_description = Single-cell RNA-seq (10x Genomics Chromium Next GEM Single Cell 5′ v2) of FACS-sorted CD45(int)CD11b(int) microglia from ASO-control-administered mouse brain on day 56 after stroke onset. ASOs were administered intracerebroventricularly on days 29 and 43 after stroke onset. Sequenced on DNBSEQ-G400.
!Sample_data_processing = Read mapping and counting were processed with the 10x Genomics Cell Ranger 6.0.1 with the mm10 reference genome assembly with the addition of dTomato RNA sequences and gene annotation provided by 10x Genomics.
!Sample_data_processing = The SC Transformation method incorporated in Seurat 4.3.0 was used for the normalization of spliced-read counts for the individual genes.
!Sample_data_processing = The single-cell gene expression profiles of the samples were integrated using the anchor-based integration method in Seurat. Ten groups with k-means were obtained by this integrated count matrix, which clustered the cells by the shared nearest neighbor approach implemented in Seurat.
!Sample_data_processing = The UMAP plots were generated with the Seurat Dimplot module by using the normalized spliced read counts.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: mm10 (GRCm38)
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Cell Ranger filtered_feature_bc_matrix output in MEX format (barcodes.tsv.gz, features.tsv.gz, matrix.mtx.gz).
!Sample_platform_id = GPL28457
